    "text": "Now let me generate a comprehensive report:

## Summary

I've found the **root cause of the Electron app freezing**. The issue is in the Tailwind CSS configuration in `/packages/ui/src/styles/index.css`.

### The Problem

The z-index CSS custom properties (`--z-splash`, `--z-modal`, `--z-dropdown`, etc.) are defined at the `:root` level, but they are **NOT included in the Tailwind v4 `@theme` block**. This means Tailwind doesn't generate the corresponding utility classes (`z-splash`, `z-modal`, etc.).

When the SplashScreen component (added/modified in recent commits) tries to use `className="fixed inset-0 z-splash flex..."`, the `z-splash` class doesn't actually exist in the compiled CSS. The SplashScreen renders as a fixed, full-screen overlay (`fixed inset-0`) with invalid z-index styling, creating a blocking layer that covers the entire UI.

### Specific Evidence

1. **File**: `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/apps/electron/src/renderer/components/SplashScreen.tsx` (Line 18)
   - Uses: `className="fixed inset-0 z-splash flex items-center justify-center bg-background"`
   - The `z-splash` class is not defined in Tailwind

2. **File**: `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/packages/ui/src/styles/index.css`
   - CSS variables are defined: `--z-splash: 600;` (Line 95)
   - But NOT in the `@theme inline` block (starting at line ~174)
   - The `@theme` block only defines color, font, and shadow tokens—no z-index tokens

3. **Additional affected classes** found in the codebase:
   - `z-modal` (used in dialog.tsx, drawer.tsx) - also not defined
   - `z-floating-backdrop`, `z-floating-menu`, `z-island`, etc. - also not defined

4. **Why it appears frozen**:
   - SplashScreen renders with `fixed inset-0` (covers full viewport)
   - Without proper z-index, it may render at `z-index: auto` or `0`
   - If another element also has `fixed inset-0`, they stack unpredictably
   - The SplashScreen's animation tries to exit, but the opacity may not change due to missing z-index context
   - This creates an invisible or semi-visible overlay that blocks all clicks

### Related Files

- `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/apps/electron/src/renderer/components/SplashScreen.tsx` - Uses `z-splash`
- `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/apps/electron/src/renderer/components/workspace/WorkspaceCreationScreen.tsx` - Uses `z-splash`
- `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/apps/electron/src/renderer/components/ui/dialog.tsx` - Uses `z-modal`
- `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/apps/electron/src/renderer/components/ui/drawer.tsx` - Uses `z-modal`
- `./Users/timokurz/Developer/craft-agents-oss/apps/electron/src/renderer/index.css` - Also defines some z-index variables

### Recent Changes

- Commit `842b759` (feat: rebrand Craft Agents → Orcha Agents) changed `CraftAgentsSymbol` to `OrchaAgentsSymbol` in SplashScreen, but this is just a component name change and not the root cause
- The real issue is that z-index Tailwind classes were never properly configured in the upstream or fork

### Solution Required

The z-index CSS variables must be added to the Tailwind `@theme` block in `/packages/ui/src/styles/index.css`:

```css
@theme inline {
  /* ... existing color, font, shadow definitions ... */

  --z-base: 0;
  --z-local: 10;
  --z-sticky: 20;
  --z-titlebar: 40;
  --z-panel: 50;
  --z-dropdown: 100;
  --z-tooltip: 150;
  --z-modal: 200;
  --z-overlay: 300;
  --z-fullscreen: 350;
  --z-floating-backdrop: 390;
  --z-floating-menu: 400;
  --z-island-overlay: 390;
  --z-island: 400;
  --z-island-popover: 410;
  --z-splash: 600;
}
```

This will enable Tailwind to generate the proper utility classes like `z-splash`, `z-modal`, etc., which will fix the app freeze."
